[{:adr/id "2607124800"
  :adr/title "cloud-itonami-isic-5820 gains real disk persistence (FileStore); DatomicStore mislabeling discovered and recorded"
  :adr/status :accepted
  :adr/date "2026-07-12"
  :db/id -1
  :adr/related ["2607124600-cloud-itonami-isic-5820-http-service-layer"]
  :adr/loop-context "Third cycle of the /loop dynamic-mode self-paced 'raise maturity toward live production operation' task."
  :adr/important-finding "crm.store/DatomicStore is NOT actually durable across a process restart despite its name and despite this fleet's repeated 'MemStore ‖ DatomicStore parity' framing in prior ADRs. Its constructor (->DatomicStore (langchain.db/create-conn schema)) resolves to a plain in-memory atom via langchain.db/create-conn -- no connection URI, socket, or file, nothing outliving the JVM heap. It is Datomic-API-shaped (via langchain.db, an in-process EAV emulation) not Datomic-backed, with the exact same lifetime as MemStore. This same naming pattern (MemStore/DatomicStore) recurs across this fleet's 140+ other cloud-itonami-isic-#### actors and may carry the same misleading implication elsewhere; this ADR intentionally scopes its fix to cloud-itonami-isic-5820 only and records the broader pattern as an unaudited, out-of-scope observation for the owner to act on separately if desired."
  :adr/decision "Did NOT wire an env-var-selected DatomicStore path (that would have been presenting fake persistence as real). Instead added src/crm/file_store.clj: a genuinely disk-durable Store implementation writing a full EDN snapshot via write-then-rename after every mutating call, reloaded on construction. crm.http/-main now reads $ISIC5820_STORE_FILE: set -> real FileStore; unset -> falls back to seed-db but now prints a loud, previously-absent stderr warning every time, so an operator can no longer accidentally run without persistence silently."
  :adr/verification-rigor "End-to-end verification went beyond unit tests: started clojure -M:serve as a real OS process against a temp file, committed data via a real POST /propose over HTTP, confirmed the file changed on disk, kill -9'd the process, restarted a fresh process against the same file, and confirmed data survival via both GET /dashboard and an independent governance check (stage-sequence-gate correctly rejecting a reverse transition, which only makes sense if the restarted process actually loaded the persisted stage state)."
  :adr/honest-scope "FileStore is explicitly documented as NOT multi-writer-safe (single-process, single-writer only, no file lock/CAS), NOT a query engine, NOT transactional history -- a snapshot persistence mechanism sufficient for single-operator/small-deployment durability, not a database replacement. A genuinely Datomic/kotoba-server-backed path remains a real follow-up requiring crm.store refactored to an injected :db-api plus a live, credentialed pod -- infrastructure unavailable in this sandbox, not faked."
  :adr/test-status "48 tests / 170 assertions (up from 45/158 pre-existing), 0 failures, lint 0 errors/0 warnings, commit 41927ea, pushed."
  :adr/remaining-gaps "No real Datomic/kotoba-server-backed durable option; cloud-itonami-isic-6201 does not yet have equivalent persistence; no multi-writer/horizontal-scale story; no real LLM; no TLS/observability; no deployment; fleet-wide DatomicStore-naming audit left unstarted."
  :adr/scope-note "New ADR because it addresses a distinct infrastructure gap (persistence) discovered while closing the honest-scope caveat from ADR-2607124600, and surfaces a genuinely new, previously-undocumented finding about DatomicStore's actual (non-)durability"}]
